Overlay patch 0036 rev2: gDPFillWideRectangle — sign-safe packing.

Two independent sign killers stacked on the same macro; rev1 fixed only
the second, which is why the device gap survived it:

(1) FLOAT->U32 SATURATION (the actual left-edge bug, rev2). Callers pass
    floats — draw_box_fill_wide feeds OTRGetDimensionFromLeftEdge(0)-1 =
    -101.57 at 2.17:1 — and _SHIFTL's first act is (u32)(v). Float ->
    unsigned of a negative value is UB; ARM64 (device AND Apple-Silicon
    sim) lowers it to fcvtzu, which SATURATES to 0. The wide rect's left
    edge therefore packed as 0 regardless of field width: the cinematic
    bars start at exactly N64 x=0 (device column 528 of 2736 — measured
    in artifacts/live-session-4k/intro-letterbox-gap.png; the "380" in
    the consult brief was read off a scaled viewer). Fix: truncate via
    (int) FIRST — float->signed truncation is defined — then let the
    (u32) wrap preserve the two's-complement bit pattern.

(2) 22-BIT SIGN TRUNCATION (rev1, kept). The interpreter handler decodes
    24-bit sign-extended ((int32_t)(C0(0,24) << 8) >> 8); packing with a
    22-bit mask drops the sign bits of negative integer coords.

Also (3): mask the packed field to 24 bits AFTER the shift — _SHIFTL
masks before shifting, so bits 24..25 of a negative coord would OR into
w0's opcode byte. Harmless for _g1 (no opcode), fatal for _g0 if a
negative lrx ever reaches the macro; make the packing total instead of
relying on callers' clamps.


--- a/libultraship/include/libultraship/libultra/gbi.h
+++ b/libultraship/include/libultraship/libultra/gbi.h
@@ -4030,10 +4030,21 @@
 #define gDPFillWideRectangle(pkt, ulx, uly, lrx, lry)                           \
     {                                                                           \
         Gfx *_g0 = (Gfx*)(pkt), *_g1 = (Gfx*)(pkt);                             \
-        _g0->words.w0 = _SHIFTL(G_FILLWIDERECT, 24, 8) | _SHIFTL((lrx), 2, 22); \
-        _g0->words.w1 = _SHIFTL((lry), 2, 22);                                  \
-        _g1->words.w0 = _SHIFTL((ulx), 2, 22);                                  \
-        _g1->words.w1 = _SHIFTL((uly), 2, 22);                                  \
+        /* SOH_IOS (overlay 0036 rev2): sign-safe packing, three parts.     \
+           (1) (int) casts: callers pass FLOATS (OTRGetDimensionFromLeftEdge \
+           yields -101.57 on 2.17:1 panels) and _SHIFTL's (u32)(v) on a      \
+           negative float is UB that ARM64 lowers to fcvtzu = saturate to 0  \
+           -> the left edge packed as 0 no matter the field width. Truncate  \
+           via (int) first (defined), then wrap to u32.                      \
+           (2) 24-bit fields, NOT 22: the interpreter decodes 24-bit         \
+           sign-extended; 22 bits dropped the sign of negative int coords.   \
+           (3) mask AFTER the shift so a negative coord's bits 24..25        \
+           can't reach w0's opcode byte. */                                  \
+        _g0->words.w0 = _SHIFTL(G_FILLWIDERECT, 24, 8) |                        \
+                        (_SHIFTL((int)(lrx), 2, 24) & 0x00FFFFFF);              \
+        _g0->words.w1 = _SHIFTL((int)(lry), 2, 24) & 0x00FFFFFF;                \
+        _g1->words.w0 = _SHIFTL((int)(ulx), 2, 24) & 0x00FFFFFF;                \
+        _g1->words.w1 = _SHIFTL((int)(uly), 2, 24) & 0x00FFFFFF;                \
     }
 
 /* Fraction never used in fill */
